place Loot_ChestSmall dcamp at 7.6 37.1 ground sit yaw=37
call airpocket x=3.1 z=33.6 id=iron_whale_decks_dair al=dairzone bub=dairbub r=2.5 msg="Air trapped in a diver's bell-tent. Breathe."
note dnote Diver's slate | A SLATE TIED TO A BOX - B. EKLUND, SHIP'S DIVER\n\nCold. Too cold for long dives. I tried singing to keep warm and a seal came to listen, which was flattering, and then left, which was honest.\nThere is air in the rooms only - under the boilers' hood, up in the shaft tunnel, in the captain's cabin. Nowhere else. Count your strokes and get out at the first shiver.\nThe captain is still in there. She knocks on the hull at seven every morning, three short and one long, so we know she is alive. I knock back with a spanner.\nIf this slate is still here, I went in after her and did not come out. Leave a lamp on the mast for me anyway.
note dcamp Diver's cache | A diver's spare kit, wired shut against the current.
loot dcamp Rope*2;Glass*3;Plastic*4
prop dcamp loot.refill=0
place TP_SnowVehicle01 dvan at -6.1 -38.5 ground yaw=157
prop dvan tint.color=#8a9aa6
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at -10.1 -35.5 ground sit yaw=97
note dwreckchest Frozen chest | Frozen to the runner: wool, rope, a tin of nails.
loot dwreckchest Wool*3;Rope*2;Nail*8
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=38.5 z=-6.1 r=15 seed=12691 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;Wool*3;Bolt*2
call vinecache x=-6.1 z=-38.5 r=15 seed=12693 chest=dvinechest vines=dvines items=Rope*3;Wool*2;Bolt*3
call treasure x=-38.5 z=6.1 r=15 n=1 seed=12692
prop treasure12692 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;MetalOre*2
# REDO 10-24 TREASURE2: a second buried treasure on the far side for the detector + shovel
call treasure x=30.8 z=-4.9 r=12 n=1 seed=12742
prop treasure12742 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*1;MetalOre*2;TradeToken*2
place Zone_Trigger dview at 33.4 20.1 ground y=1.5
prop dview zone.id=iron_whale_decks_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=The stern lies on the seabed below, dark red, its rooms full of water and silence.


# --- DEEP 10-24: the propeller trench, the funnel, the stokers' cave ---
note trenchchest Propeller locker | The shaft crew's locker, thrown clear: spanners, a lamp, grease.
loot trenchchest MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;TitaniumOre*1
note funnelchest Funnel locker | The fireman's locker inside the funnel's lip: dry and untouched.
loot funnelchest MetalIngot*3;Bolt*3;TradeToken*2
note stokertally Stoker's tally | STOKER'S TALLY - O. BERG, LEADING STOKER\n\nCoal in: forty sacks. Coal out: thirty-eight. The two good sacks are in the cave, and the Chief does not know, and if the Chief is reading this, hello, Chief, it was the cook.\nWe fed her day and night when the ice came. She drank coal like a sailor drinks on shore leave and she still could not shove the ridge.\nThe stern will go. Every stoker knows the sound a hull makes before it lets go, a long groan like a cow in a cold barn. I heard it twice last night.\nIf she ever goes down, do not swim for the hatches - they jam. Go up the funnel. The funnel always stands. It is the only honest thing on a ship.
note stokerchest Stokers' stash | Under the coal sacks: a kettle, tins, a flask.
loot stokerchest Scrap*3;Rope*2;Raw_GenericMeat*2
prop stokerchest loot.refill=0
prop treasure12801 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*1;CopperOre*2;MetalOre*2

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest -----------------------------------------------------------------
# the generator's rocks that floated over the slope (ground check, 2026-10-23)
clear at -8.2 -10.57 r=1.5 only=TP_BigRock
clear at -9.41 29.56 r=1.5 only=TP_BigRock
clear at 6.38 -15.34 r=1.5 only=TP_BigRock

info title=The Iron Whale - Engine Decks
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Whale's stern, broken off and sunk at the ridge: flooded engine rooms, a boiler hall and a shaft tunnel with air under their deckheads, anglers in the dark - and the stern mast standing out of the sea, a wind turbine on it. The captain is still aboard. The sixth island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||A mast standing out of the sea, a turbine on it turning slowly. Under you, deep down, the Whale's stern - and a lamp in one of her ports.

story fuse|A breaker fuse|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A heavy ceramic fuse from the Whale's spares, three of them sit in the main breaker.
story galleycode|The officers' safe code|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The mess code opened the officers' safe too.
story breaker|The main breaker|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The Whale's main breaker, thrown: her lights burn again from stern to bow.
story heddakey|Hedda's cage key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The key to the cage in the captain's room, from her strongbox.

note captainslog40 Captain's log, day 40 | THE IRON WHALE - CAPTAIN'S LOG\n\nDay 40. The stern went in the night - she broke at the ridge like a biscuit. The crew went forward over the ice to the bow. I stayed: the charts are here, and the vault's bearings with them, and the hand key, and Ylva.\nLunde shouted at me through the hatch for an hour. He has a good voice for shouting. I told him a captain stays with the part of her ship that still has a radio.\nI've locked myself in my room. There is air, and rations for a while. The keycard is in the chief's locker - whoever comes, come. Bring something hot. Bring anything at all.\n\n- H. Brask
note heddasaccount Hedda Brask's account | (written small, on the back of a chart)\n\nThe flotilla city went quiet first. Saga Drift - nine ships lashed together, the best radio on the white sea. One day: nothing. Then the Steamvent band, then the relay. The Coldhold said keep silent, and everyone did.\nI did not. Ylva and I tapped short bursts on the hand key - a few seconds, never on the hour - so the vault could not fix us. If you heard a woman reading the ice on the air, that was me. I sent those fragments. I would send them again.\nThe courier came aboard that week. I gave him my last coffee. Two nights later the aerial was cut and the stern cable chopped through.\nGo to Saga Drift, 900. Find out who gave the order.\n\n- Hedda Brask, master of the Iron Whale
note enginestore Engine store | Engine room store: the advanced battery's plans, cells packed in wax.
note chiefslocker Chief engineer's locker | Chief's locker: headlight plans, spanners, the captain's keycard on a lanyard.
note shaftbox Shaft box | Bolted to the shaft wall: stern gland tools, iron for patches.
note galley Officers' galley | Officers' galley: the grill's plans. Taped inside: SAFE = SAME AS THE MESS.
note officersafe Officers' safe | The officers' safe: their pay, a spare cell, copper wire.
note sundnote The radio officer | (on a signal pad, in pencil, by the switch) - Y. SUND, RADIO OFFICER\n\nDay 39. The bow's aerial was cut on the 31st and the stern cable chopped the same night, so I am working the hand key into the stern mast's wire, which is held on with a bootlace and prayer. The captain taps; I keep the battery warm inside my coat. It is the most romantic thing I have ever done with a battery.\nThe hull groans every hour now. The stokers say that means she will go soon. Stokers say a lot of things.\nIf she goes, I will hold this switch down until the last burst is out. Somebody on 900 might still be listening. Somebody on the ice might hear the captain and come.\nTell my sister the cards are in my bunk. All forty-one.
note cablenote Radio cable, chopped | CHIEF'S TAG, TIED TO THE CABLE - M. DAHL, CHIEF ENGINEER\n\nFound like this the night of the 31st, by the light of my pipe. The stern's radio cable chopped through in two blows, and the hatchet still in it - left behind in a hurry, like a man who heard my boots on the ladder.\nIt is not one of ours. Our axes are red and stamped WHALE. This one is old and loved, its handle carved like a dog's head, ears back, worn smooth by somebody's thumb.\nI have not pulled it out. The captain says leave it, so whoever owns it knows we have seen it.\nThe order to keep silent came on Saga Drift's band, on 900. If you want to know who is behind this, start there.
prop radiozone zone.id=radio_corner
prop radiozone zone.radius=2.5
prop radiozone zone.repeat=never
prop radiozone zone.message=The radio corner. Officer Sund sits at the switch, her hand still on it, long dead. Beside her, a hatchet in the cable.
loot officersafe TradeToken*5;Battery*1;CopperIngot*3;Bolt*2
prop officersafe loot.refill=0
prop officersafe obj.name=officersafe
prop officersafe if.open=signal|galleycode
prop officersafe else.open=message||The officers' safe is locked. The keypad beside it wants a code - the same as the mess, says the card.
prop galleypad obj.name=galleypad
prop galleypad beh.use=Type the officers' safe code
prop galleypad lock.code=4127
prop galleypad on.use=sound||event:/exploring/obstacles/keypad/keypad_correct\nmessage||The keypad beeps. The officers' safe opens.\nsignal||galleycode\ngive||story:galleycode*1
prop galleypad else.use=message||Four digits. The card in the galley locker says: same as the mess.
note mastbox Mast box | The mast's box, iced over: the wind turbine's plans.
loot enginestore Blueprint_BatteryAdvanced*1;story:fuse*1;Battery*1;CopperIngot*2
prop enginestore loot.refill=0
loot chiefslocker Blueprint_HeadLight_Advanced*1;story:raft-Tangaroa_KeyCard*1;story:fuse*1;Bolt*3
prop chiefslocker loot.refill=0
loot shaftbox story:fuse*1;MetalIngot*3;Scrap*4;Hinge*2
prop shaftbox loot.refill=0
loot galley Blueprint_ElectricGrill*1;Raw_GenericMeat*2;Bucket*1
prop galley loot.refill=0
loot mastbox Blueprint_WindTurbine*1;CircuitBoard*1;Rope*2
prop mastbox loot.refill=0
loot captvault story:heddakey*1;TradeToken*4;MetalIngot*2
prop captvault loot.refill=0
prop captvault note.title=Captain's room
prop captvault beh.hidden=1

prop mastzone zone.id=stern_mast
prop mastzone zone.radius=4
prop mastzone zone.message=The stern mast. Below you, green-black, the Whale's stern on the ridge.
prop hulldark atmo.fog=#05090c
prop hulldark atmo.fogAmount=0.6
prop hulldark atmo.light=#1a2a30
prop hulldark atmo.lightAmount=0.5
prop hulldark atmo.particles=mist
prop hulldark zone.radius=14
prop anglers creature.count=3
prop anglers creature.respawn=0
prop anglers creature.zone=engine_room

prop captdoor obj.name=captdoor
prop captdoor on.use=hide|\nshow|captvault\nmessage||The reader blinks green. The captain's door swings in - air, a lamp, a cage.
prop heddacage obj.name=heddacage
prop heddacage survivor.name=Hedda
prop heddacage survivor.id=frozen_hedda
prop heddacage survivor.key=heddakey
prop heddacage survivor.signal=heddafree
prop heddacage survivor.line=I locked myself in against the anglers and threw the key in my strongbox. Foolish. Thank you. Read what I wrote - Saga Drift first.
prop mainbreaker obj.name=mainbreaker
prop mainbreaker beh.use=Throw the main breaker
prop mainbreaker if.use=!signal|power\ntake|story:fuse|3
prop mainbreaker else.use=message||The breaker is dead - three fuse holders, all empty. The spares were split up: engine store, chief's locker, shaft box.
prop mainbreaker on.use=message||A thump through the whole hull - and far off, up on the ridge, the bow's lamps come on one by one.\nsignal||power\ngive||story:breaker*1\nshow|deckslights
prop deckslights beh.hidden=1

